# ANY live root or archive of one, WHATEVER IT IS CALLED. 2026-09-16: run 1's
# archived root sat at the repo root as archive-contaminated-20260913-1244/
# and an unscoped `git add -A` shipped 80 files of it -- journal, engine log,
# the creature's tools -- to the public repo. `live/` above guarded a path,
# not the thing. These guard the names a root can have; the gate guards the
# CONTENT (test_no_live_root_is_tracked_by_git_whatever_it_is_called).
archive-*/
*-archive-*/
live-*/
